message: "If you use this workflow, please cite it using the metadata below."

title: "PCR Assay Design and In Silico Validation Workflow"

type: software

authors:
  - family-names: "Faham"
    given-names: "Aymane"

version: 1.2.0

date-released: 2026-09-02

license: GPL-3.0-or-later

repository-code: "https://github.com/Epigenome-Sb/PCR-assay-design-workflow"

url: "https://github.com/Epigenome-Sb/PCR-assay-design-workflow"

abstract: >-
  An interactive and reproducible command-line workflow for nucleotide
  sequence preprocessing, multiple sequence alignment, conservation analysis,
  PCR assay design with VarVAMP, and in silico validation. The workflow
  supports VarVAMP SINGLE, QPCR, and TILED modes and integrates MAFFT, MARS,
  SeqKit, CD-HIT-EST, trimAl, VarVAMP, MFEprimer, and BLAST+. It provides
  explicit scientific parameter checkpoints, run-specific provenance,
  primer-pair target-coverage analysis, and detailed evaluation of qPCR
  probes, including expansion and comparison of existing IUPAC-degenerate
  probe variants.

keywords:
  - PCR
  - qPCR
  - primer design
  - probe design
  - in silico validation
